axtb in ReShiki
===============

Component:  axtb, an implementation of the xTB methods (GFN2-xTB, GFN-FF, g-xTB)
License:    LGPL-3.0-or-later (COPYING.LESSER, with the GPL-3.0 text in COPYING)
Upstream:   https://github.com/atomsforhumanity/axtb (Colton Hicks)
Fork:       https://github.com/Ameyanagi/axtb, branch reshiki
Revision:   9d0388c9e9d81c43c0e7bba01c0ccf706a88fc91
Version:    0.2.0
Crates:     axtb, axtb-base, axtb-d4, axtb-driver, axtb-gfnff, axtb-gxtb,
            axtb-solvation; with the fork's patched copies of the MIT crates
            gemm-common and private-gemm-x86 (third_party/ in the fork)

The fork is a modified version of axtb. The files COPYING, COPYING.LESSER,
NOTICE and CHANGES-reshiki.md here are copied unchanged from that revision.
NOTICE lists the upstream projects axtb reproduces and the g-xTB authors'
permission for its g-xTB parts. CHANGES-reshiki.md is the fork's notice of
modification: what changed relative to upstream commit
65d0f64a9a8211f73b0738ff908b7a414975f50b (axtb 0.2.0), and when.

The macOS and Linux desktop releases contain axtb through the Cargo feature
`xtb`. The separate Python package `reshiki-xtb` also contains axtb. The base
Python package `reshiki` excludes it. Each release that contains
axtb publishes reshiki-<version>-source.tar.gz on the GitHub release of the
same version (https://github.com/Ameyanagi/ReShiki/releases/tag/v<version>),
containing ReShiki's source, this revision of the fork, every Cargo dependency,
and BUILD-WITH-XTB.md with the steps to rebuild the application and Python
worker wheel, including with a modified axtb.
